r; 5 none), the 3D grass (density multiplier, metres from the camera) and the map's decals, water, local fog and particles leaves and grass brought to measured colours (0 the textures' own, 1 a real leaf's: some 4 to 12 % of the light back, an olive green, not a painted one; NFX_LitData) --- added in config version 62: the debug page (Tools/DebugPage.cs) --- sky: HDRP volumetric clouds following the weather (and the map's cloud sea), the strength of their shadows, the blue haze over distant mountains (0 off) the sky drawn by NatureFX's own engine (physically based atmosphere) over HDRP's the fog and haze drawn by the own engine (lit by the traced sun and the engine's sky) instead of HDRP's all of the opaque lighting from the own engine (roadmap step A): its shadows, lamp shadows, sky light and GI, reflections, whatever the ray tracing toggles say (Rendering.EngineLighting) how bright the own engine's stars are against their physical brightness (the eye's night vision, which the camera's exposure does not reach), and how long a change of weather takes (s) falling rain (with splashes) and snow around the camera: how dense (0 off) shader rebuild: hex tiled textures where the map's [materials] ask for it (antitiling=), 0 off .. 1 cars: NatureFX's lit volumetric tyre smoke and spray (amount, 0 off), whether it replaces the game's own smoke on DX11 (on DX12 the game has none), glowing brake discs and afterfire""},""CarDirt"":{""label"":""Dirt, dust and snow on the car"",""help"":""Builds up as you drive: mud on wet roads, dust on dusty ones, snow on top while it snows. Rain washes it off.""},""CarDirtAmount"":{""label"":""Most dirt"",""help"":""map extension (docs/map-authoring.md 5 and 7): season of the foliage colours and the floating particles (0 automatic: the weather preset, else the map's [defaults] season; 1 spring .. 4 winter; 5 none), the 3D grass (density multiplier, metres from the camera) and the map's decals, water, local fog and particles leaves and grass brought to measured colours (0 the textures' own, 1 a real leaf's: some 4 to 12 % of the light back, an olive green, not a painted one; NFX_LitData) --- added in config version 62: the debug page (Tools/DebugPage.cs) --- sky: HDRP volumetric clouds following the weather (and the map's cloud sea), the strength of their shadows, the blue haze over distant mountains (0 off) the sky drawn by NatureFX's own engine (physically based atmosphere) over HDRP's the fog and haze drawn by the own engine (lit by the traced sun and the engine's sky) instead of HDRP's all of the opaque lighting from the own engine (roadmap step A): its shadows, lamp shadows, sky light and GI, reflections, whatever the ray tracing toggles say (Rendering.EngineLighting) how bright the own engine's stars are against their physical brightness (the eye's night vision, which the camera's exposure does not reach), and how long a change of weather takes (s) falling rain (with splashes) and snow around the camera: how dense (0 off) shader rebuild: hex tiled textures where the map's [materials] ask for it (antitiling=), 0 off .. 1 cars: NatureFX's lit volumetric tyre smoke and spray (amount, 0 off), whether it replaces the game's own smoke on DX11 (on DX12 the game has none), glowing brake discs and afterfire dirt, dust and snow building up on the car nearest the camera (how much at most)""},""RTReflections"":{""label"":""Enable"",""help"":""ray traced reflections (DX12, DXR)""},""RTReflectionIntensity"":{""label"":""Strength"",""help"":""ray traced reflections (DX12, DXR)""},""RTReflectionRoughness"":{""label"":""Rough surfaces up to"",""help"":""surfaces rougher than this get none""},""RTReflectionDistance"":{""label"":""Ray length"",""help"":""ray traced reflections (DX12, DXR)""},""RTReflectionQuality"":{""label"":""Ray traced reflections"",""help"":""0 performance, 1 balanced, 2 quality""},""RTGlassReflections"":{""label"":""Glass reflections"",""help"":""Car windows, lamp lenses and building windows mirror the scene.""},""RTGlassRefraction"":{""label"":""Glass refraction"",""help"":""How much curved glass (lenses, screens) bends what is seen through it. 0: off.""},""RTWetReflections"":{""label"":""Wet road streaks"",""help"":""When the road is wet (Weather: wetness or rain), reflections of lamps and cars stretch along the view as on real wet asphalt.""},""NativeGlass"":{""label"":""Own glass"",""help"":""roadmap E: the own engine draws the glass whole (HDRP's hidden)""},""NativePost"":{""label"":""Own post-processing"",""help"":""roadmap D: NatureFX's own exposure, bloom, tone curve and colour""},""PostBloom"":{""label"":""Bloom"",""help"":""The share of all light a lens and the eye scatter around: bright lamps glow, a grey wall hardly at all (no threshold).""},""ExposureMode"":{""label"":""Exposure"",""help"":""0 fixed (FixedExposure), 1 eye adaptation""},""FixedExposure"":{""label"":""Fixed exposure"",""help"":""Real-world EV: a sunny day about 15, overcast 12, a lit street at night about 3.""},""AutoExposureMin"":{""label"":""Darkest scene"",""help"":""EV100""},""AutoExposureMax"":{""label"":""Brightest scene"",""help"":""Real-world EV: a sunny day is about 15, a lit street at night about 3, a moonlit night about -2. Darkest scene is how far the eye opens up at night: lower lets a moonlit night show.""},""AdaptationSpeed"":{""label"":""Adaptation speed"",""help"":""--- added in config version 5: camera realism ---""},""NightDarkness"":{""label"":""Night seen dark"",""help"":""The eye does not lift a dark scene to grey: about 2 stops darker under street lamps, 3.5 in a dark night. 0: every scene as bright as day.""},""Exposure"":{""label"":""Exposure compensation"",""help"":""exposure and tone (ray tracing only mode, VolumeOverhaul)""},""AcesTonemapping"":{""label"":""Override tonemapping"",""help"":""exposure and tone (ray tracing only mode, VolumeOverhaul)""},""TonemapMode"":{""label"":""Tone"",""help"":""0 ACES, 1 Neutral (Khronos PBR Neutral), 2 AgX, 3 None""},""Contrast"":{""label"":""Contrast"",""help"":""exposure and tone (ray tracing only mode, VolumeOverhaul)""},""Saturation"":{""label"":""Saturation"",""help"":""Like a camera: AgX, contrast 8, saturation 0 (highlights turn white, bright colours do not clip). Neutral keeps the surfaces' colours saturated up to white.""},""WhiteBalance"":{""label"":""White balance (eye)"",""help"":""How much the eye takes the light around as white: a sunset or warm lamps less orange, a shade under a blue sky less blue. 0: the camera's daylight white. Less in the dark, as the eye. Needs Own post-processing.""},""Dlaa"":{""label"":""NVIDIA DLSS"",""help"":""NVIDIA DLSS (own engine) in place of HDRP's TAA, with the own post""},""DlssQuality"":{""label"":""NVIDIA DLSS"",""help"":""0 DLAA, 1 Quality, 2 Balanced, 3 Performance, 4 Ultra performance (upscaling)""},""DlssRayReconstruction"":{""label"":""Ray Reconstruction"",""help"":""DLSS denoises the ray traced sun shadows with the whole picture, in place of NRD and NatureFX's filter (reflections, ambient light, GI and lamp shadows keep theirs). Needs the exact sun light (Shadows). DLAA: anti-aliasing at the display resolution. Quality, Balanced, Performance, Ultra perf.: rendered at 67, 58, 50, 33 % of it and upscaled (faster; the sun shadows get 2 to 4 rays a pixel to keep their quality). At 1080p Quality or Balanced; Ultra perf. is for 4K and above.""},""NightVision"":{""label"":""Night vision"",""help"":""map extension (docs/map-authoring.md 5 and 7): season of the foliage colours and the floating particles (0 automatic: the weather preset, else the map's [defaults] season; 1 spring .. 4 winter; 5 none), the 3D grass (density multiplier, metres from the camera) and the map's decals, water, local fog and particles leaves and grass brought to measured colours (0 the textures' own, 1 a real leaf's: some 4 to 12 % of the light back, an olive green, not a painted one; NFX_LitData) --- added in config version 62: the debug page (Tools/DebugPage.cs) --- sky: HDRP volumetric clouds following the weather (and the map's cloud sea), the strength of their shadows, the blue haze over distant mountains (0 off) the sky drawn by NatureFX's own engine (physically based atmosphere) over HDRP's the fog and haze drawn by the own engine (lit by the traced sun and the engine's sky) instead of HDRP's all of the opaque lighting from the own engine (roadmap step A): its shadows, lamp shadows, sky light and GI, reflections, whatever the ray tracing toggles say (Rendering.EngineLighting) how bright the own engine's stars are against their physical brightness (the eye's night vision, which the camera's exposure does not reach), and how long a change of weather takes (s) falling rain (with splashes) and snow around the camera: how dense (0 off) shader rebuild: hex tiled textures where the map's [materials] ask for it (antitiling=), 0 off .. 1 cars: NatureFX's lit volumetric tyre smoke and spray (amount, 0 off), whether it replaces the game's own smoke on DX11 (on DX12 the game has none), glowing brake discs and afterfire dirt, dust and snow building up on the car nearest the camera (how much at most) the camera and the eye: night vision (Purkinje shift and grain, 0 off), lens flare (0 off), depth of field on the car nearest the camera""},""LensFlare"":{""label"":""Lens flare"",""help"":""map extension (docs/map-authoring.md 5 and 7): season of the foliage colours and the floating particles (0 automatic: the weather preset, else the map's [defaults] season; 1 spring .. 4 winter; 5 none), the 3D grass (density multiplier, metres from the camera) and the map's decals, water, local fog and particles leaves and grass brought to measured colours (0 the textures' own, 1 a real leaf's: some 4 to 12 % of the light back, an olive green, not a painted one; NFX_LitData) --- added in config version 62: the debug page (Tools/DebugPage.cs) --- sky: HDRP volumetric clouds following the weather (and the map's cloud sea), the strength of their shadows, the blue haze over distant mountains (0 off) the sky drawn by NatureFX's own engine (physically based atmosphere) over HDRP's the fog and haze drawn by the own engine (lit by the traced sun and the engine's sky) instead of HDRP's all of the opaque lighting from the own engine (roadmap step A): its shadows, lamp shadows, sky light and GI, reflections, whatever the ray tracing toggles say (Rendering.EngineLighting) how bright the own engine's stars are against their physical brightness (the eye's night vision, which the camera's exposure does not reach), and how long a change of weather takes (s) falling rain (with splashes) and snow around the camera: how dense (0 off) shader rebuild: hex tiled textures where the map's [materials] ask for it (antitiling=), 0 off .. 1 cars: NatureFX's lit volumetric tyre smoke and spray (amount, 0 off), whether it replaces the game's own smoke on DX11 (on DX12 the game has none), glowing brake discs and afterfire dirt, dust and snow building up on the car nearest the camera (how much at most) the camera and the eye: night vision (Purkinje shift and grain, 0 off), lens flare (0 off), depth of field on the car nearest the camera""},""LensStreaks"":{""label"":""Light streaks"",""help"":""map extension (docs/map-authoring.md 5 and 7): season of the foliage colours and the floating particles (0 automatic: the weather preset, else the map's [defaults] season; 1 spring .. 4 winter; 5 none), the 3D grass (density multiplier, metres from the camera) and the map's decals, water, local fog and particles leaves and grass brought to measured colours (0 the textures' own, 1 a real leaf's: some 4 to 12 % of the light back, an olive green, not a painted one; NFX_LitData) --- added in config version 62: the debug page (Tools/DebugPage.cs) --- sky: HDRP volumetric clouds following the weather (and the map's cloud sea), the strength of their shadows, the blue haze over distant mountains (0 off) the sky drawn by NatureFX's own engine (physically based atmosphere) over HDRP's the fog and haze drawn by the own engine (lit by the traced sun and the engine's sky) instead of HDRP's all of the opaque lighting from the own engine (roadmap step A): its shadows, lamp shadows, sky light and GI, reflections, whatever the ray tracing toggles say (Rendering.EngineLighting) how bright the own engine's stars are against their physical brightness (the eye's night vision, which the camera's exposure does not reach), and how long a change of weather takes (s) falling rain (with splashes) and snow around the camera: how dense (0 off) shader rebuild: hex tiled textures where the map's [materials] ask for it (antitiling=), 0 off .. 1 cars: NatureFX's lit volumetric tyre smoke and spray (amount, 0 off), whether it replaces the game's own smoke on DX11 (on DX12 the game has none), glowing brake discs and afterfire dirt, dust and snow building up on the car nearest the camera (how much at most) the camera and the eye: night vision (Purkinje shift and grain, 0 off), lens flare (0 off), depth of field on the car nearest the camera""},""DepthOfField"":{""label"":""Depth of field"",""help"":""map extension (docs/map-authoring.md 5 and 7): season of the foliage colours and the floating particles (0 automatic: the weather preset, else the map's [defaults] season; 1 spring .. 4 winter; 5 none), the 3D grass (density multiplier, metres from the camera) and the map's decals, water, local fog and particles leaves and grass brought to measured colours (0 the textures' own, 1 a real leaf's: some 4 to 12 % of the light back, an olive green, not a painted one; NFX_LitData) --- added in config version 62: the debug page (Tools/DebugPage.cs) --- sky: HDRP volumetric clouds following the weather (and the map's cloud sea), the strength of their shadows, the blue haze over distant mountains (0 off) the sky drawn by NatureFX's own engine (physically based atmosphere) over HDRP's the fog and haze drawn by the own engine (lit by the traced sun and the engine's sky) instead of HDRP's all of the opaque lighting from the own engine (roadmap step A): its shadows, lamp shadows, sky light and GI, reflections, whatever the ray tracing toggles say (Rendering.EngineLighting) how bright the own engine's stars are against their physical brightness (the eye's night vision, which the camera's exposure does not reach), and how long a change of weather takes (s) falling rain (with splashes) and snow around the camera: how dense (0 off) shader rebuild: hex tiled textures where the map's [materials] ask for it (antitiling=), 0 off .. 1 cars: NatureFX's lit volumetric tyre smoke and spray (amount, 0 off), whether it replaces the game's own smoke on DX11 (on DX12 the game has none), glowing brake discs and afterfire dirt, dust and snow building up on the car nearest the camera (how much at most) the camera and the eye: night vision (Purkinje shift and grain, 0 off), lens flare (0 off), depth of field on the car nearest the camera the map's reflection probes (markers and along the road; off: HDRP's own reflections only) draw the map's markers over the picture (F8 > Map), for map authors""},""DofFStop"":{""label"":""Aperture"",""help"":""A real lens focused on the car nearest the camera: a low f-number blurs the background more (f/1.4 to f/2.8 a portrait look, f/8 and up nearly everything sharp).""},""MotionBlur"":{""label"":""Motion blur"",""help"":""How long the shutter stays open, as a share of a frame: 0.5 is a film camera's 180° shutter, 0 off. The chased car stays sharp, the road streams past.""},""RTAO"":{""label"":""Enable"",""help"":""ray traced ambient occlusion (DX12, DXR): darkens the light that does not come from the sun""},""RTGIBounce"":{""label"":""Bounce light"",""help"":""Surfaces pass on their colour and the sun they catch (a red wall tints the road, sunlit tarmac lights the underside of a car). Off: blocking only (ambient occlusion), lighter.""},""RTGIMultiBounce"":{""label"":""Global illumination (every bounce)"",""help"":""Own engine only: light keeps bouncing (floor to wall to ceiling under a roof), lit signs and lamps light their surroundings. Builds up over a few seconds in a world space cache. Off: one bounce.""},""RTGIDistance"":{""label"":""GI distance"",""help"":""own engine: GI ray length (m)""},""RTGIIntensity"":{""label"":""Bounce intensity"",""help"":""own engine: strength of the light GI bounces in""},""SkyLightStrength"":{""label"":""Sky light in the shade"",""help"":""How bright the sky makes what the sun does not reach (with the sky light from the own engine, Sky & fog). 1: as the sky is.""},""SkyLightSaturation"":{""label"":""Sky light colour"",""help"":""How blue the sky's light is in the shade: 1 as the sky model gives it, 0.5 as measured under a clear sky. How strongly the light bounced in (and its colour) is added; 1 is physically right.""},""RTAOStrength"":{""label"":""Strength"",""help"":""ray traced ambient occlusion (DX12, DXR): darkens the light that does not come from the sun""},""RTAODistance"":{""label"":""Distance"",""help"":""How far the light is traced: short for contact shadows in gaps, long for the shade under roofs and trees and bounce from further away.""},""RTSkyOcclusion"":{""label"":""Sky occlusion"",""help"":""Roofs and overhangs further away than the distance still take the sky (the crowd under a stand's roof). 0: off.""},""RTContactShadows"":{""label"":""Contact shadows"",""help"":""Darkens the creases where surfaces meet: barriers on the road, seat rows, wheel arches. Works best with the ray traced shadows on: then only the light that is not sunlight is darkened.""},""AntiTiling"":{""label"":""Anti-tiling"",""help"":""Hex tiles against a texture's visible repeat and seams, on the materials the map's profile asks for (antitiling=). Three texture reads instead of one there.""},""WetGameMaterials"":{""label"":""Wet look on unreplaced HDRP/Lit"",""help"":""Materials left with the game's shaders still get wet in the rain.""},""RTBackend"":{""label"":""Ray tracing engine"",""help"":""how the own engine traces: 0 DXR 1.0 (ray tracing pipelines), 1 DXR 1.1 (inline)""},""RTTraceScale"":{""label"":""Ray tracing engine"",""help"":""ambient / GI / lamp shadows: 0 half resolution, 1 quarter (upscaled over frames)""},""RTDenoiser"":{""label"":""Ray tracing engine"",""help"":""Timings, rays, lamps, the scene and GPU memory: the debug page (Developer > Debug page, in a browser).""},""RTDxr12Sun"":{""label"":""Sun shadows on DXR 1.2 (test)"",""help"":""Stage 1 of the move to DXR 1.2: the sun shadows are traced on a Shader Model 6.9 device next to the game's. Same look; compare the frame rate.""},""UiLargeText"":{""label"":""Larger text"",""help"":""F8 window: background opacity, scale and size (0 = default)""},""DebugPage"":{""label"":""Debug page"",""help"":""a page with memory, timings and the log, for a browser on this PC""},""UseMapProfile"":{""label"":""Use map profiles"",""help"":""map profiles (kino/config/NatureFX/maps/<scene>.nfx)""},""ShowMarkers"":{""label"":""Show markers"",""help"":""Draws every marker over the picture: zones, fog, particle boxes, puddles, decals, probes and lights, with what each is doing. The map has its own profile too; this file overrides it.""},""MapProbes"":{""label"":""Map reflection probes"",""help"":""Reflection probes at the map's markers and along the road (redrawn when the time or the weather changes).""},""GrassDensity"":{""label"":""3D grass density"",""help"":""map extension (docs/map-authoring.md 5 and 7): season of the foliage colours and the floating particles (0 automatic: the weather preset, else the map's [defaults] season; 1 spring .. 4 winter; 5 none), the 3D grass (density multiplier, metres from the camera) and the map's decals, water, local fog and particles leaves and grass brought to measured colours (0 the textures' own, 1 a real leaf's: some 4 to 12 % of the light back, an olive green, not a painted one; NFX_LitData)""},""GrassDistance"":{""label"":""3D grass distance"",""help"":""map extension (docs/map-authoring.md 5 and 7): season of the foliage colours and the floating particles (0 automatic: the weather preset, else the map's [defaults] season; 1 spring .. 4 winter; 5 none), the 3D grass (density multiplier, metres from the camera) and the map's decals, water, local fog and particles leaves and grass brought to measured colours (0 the textures' own, 1 a real leaf's: some 4 to 12 % of the light back, an olive green, not a painted one; NFX_LitData)""},""ShrubDensity"":{""label"":""Thicket density"",""help"":""the map's thickets of scanned shrubs (ShrubRenderer): density, 0 off""},""ShrubDistance"":{""label"":""Scanned shrubs up to"",""help"":""m: where the scans give way to their billboard clouds (impostors at 3x)""},""MapGroundDetail"":{""label"":""Ground detail"",""help"":""the ground map: ground blend, painted dirt and debris on the map""},""Detritus"":{""label"":""Debris (pebbles, twigs, leaves)"",""help"":""debris (pebbles, twigs, leaves) along the road's edges: density, 0 off""},""MapEffects"":{""label"":""Map effects"",""help"":""Local fog: Particles:""},""Enabled"":{""label"":""Enabled"",""help"":""general""},""AccumulateOverTime"":{""label"":""AccumulateOverTime"",""help"":""accumulation / weather""},""AccumulationRate"":{""label"":""AccumulationRate"",""help"":""accumulation / weather""},""Snow"":{""label"":""Snow"",""help"":""accumulation / weather""},""Leaves"":{""label"":""Leaves"",""help"":""accumulation / weather""},""Dust"":{""label"":""Dust"",""help"":""accumulation / weather""},""Wetness"":{""label"":""Wetness"",""help"":""accumulation / weather""},""ReplaceShaders"":{""label"":""ReplaceShaders"",""help"":""shader replacement (needs naturefx.bundle)""},""FullReplacement"":{""label"":""FullReplacement"",""help"":""shader rebuild: every game material becomes a NatureFX one""},""TimeSpeed"":{""label"":""TimeSpeed"",""help"":""how much faster than real time (60: an hour a minute)""},""Rain"":{""label"":""Rain"",""help"":""0..1 ripples, drips, wet surfaces""},""SunSize"":{""label"":""SunSize"",""help"":""angular diameter in degrees (PCSS, needs High shadow filtering)""},""MoonBrightness"":{""label"":""MoonBrightness"",""help"":""the moon's light against its physical strength (1 = real)""},""HeadlightKelvin"":{""label"":""HeadlightKelvin"",""help"":""the lamps' colour temperature (K); 0: the type's own""},""RecordShaderVariants"":{""label"":""RecordShaderVariants"",""help"":""development: log the NatureFX shader variants the game uses, so the bundle build can skip the rest""},""UiOpacity"":{""label"":""UiOpacity"",""help"":""F8 window: background opacity, scale and size (0 = default)""},""UiScale"":{""label"":""UiScale"",""help"":""F8 window: background opacity, scale and size (0 = default)""},""UiWidth"":{""label"":""UiWidth"",""help"":""F8 window: background opacity, scale and size (0 = default)""},""UiHeight"":{""label"":""UiHeight"",""help"":""F8 window: background opacity, scale and size (0 = default)""},""RTShadows"":{""label"":""RTShadows"",""help"":""ray traced sun shadows (DX12, DXR); softness from SunSize""},""RTShadowStrength"":{""label"":""RTShadowStrength"",""help"":""ray traced sun shadows (DX12, DXR); softness from SunSize""},""RTShadowFullRes"":{""label"":""RTShadowFullRes"",""help"":""full resolution (sharp contact shadows) or half""},""RTExactSun"":{""label"":""RTExactSun"",""help"":""take away exactly the sun light HDRP added (G-buffer drawn again)""},""RTLampMasks"":{""label"":""RTLampMasks"",""help"":""roadmap A4: each lamp shadowed by its own mask (with RTExactSun)""},""RTFullRelight"":{""label"":""RTFullRelight"",""help"":""roadmap A4: HDRP's pixel taken apart and lit again by the own engine""},""RTHideFakeShadows"":{""label"":""RTHideFakeShadows"",""help"":""hide the game's painted shadow planes while the ray traced shadows run""},""RebuildFoliage"":{""label"":""RebuildFoliage"",""help"":""shader rebuild: foliage too (wind, snow); off leaves it to the game's shaders""},""RTWind"":{""label"":""RTWind"",""help"":""own engine: the traced foliage sways with the wind as it is drawn""},""RTLeafTranslucency"":{""label"":""RTLeafTranslucency"",""help"":""sunlight through back-lit leaves (0: off)""},""RTShafts"":{""label"":""RTShafts"",""help"":""ray traced light shafts""},""RTShaftDensity"":{""label"":""RTShaftDensity"",""help"":""scattering of the air (1/m)""},""RTShaftAnisotropy"":{""label"":""RTShaftAnisotropy"",""help"":""forward scattering""},""RTLocalLights"":{""label"":""RTLocalLights"",""help"":""headlights and lamps in the ray traced effects""},""RTLampShadows"":{""label"":""RTLampShadows"",""help"":""lamps' HDRP shadow maps off, soft ray traced shadows instead""},""RTEmissiveLights"":{""label"":""RTEmissiveLights"",""help"":""bright emissive surfaces (neon, signs) light their surroundings, with shadows""},""RTGlassShadows"":{""label"":""RTGlassShadows"",""help"":""the sun through glass is dimmed (tinted windows more)""},""RTOverlay"":{""label"":""RTOverlay"",""help"":""on-screen timings, ray counts and memory""},""DebugPagePort"":{""label"":""DebugPagePort"",""help"":""its port on 127.0.0.1""},""TextureStreamingBudget"":{""label"":""TextureStreamingBudget"",""help"":""MB for Unity's texture mip streaming; 0 the game's own""},""WriteMaterialInventory"":{""label"":""WriteMaterialInventory"",""help"":""the shader rebuild's data at each map load (text and texture samples)""},""RTTransparentShadows"":{""label"":""RTTransparentShadows"",""help"":""the sun's ray traced shadow on transparent surfaces (SunShadowMap)""}},""groups"":{""Sky & fog / Sky"":{""name"":""Sky & fog / Sky"",""help"":""The sky computed by NatureFX's own engine from the sun or the moon and the air (physically based), with its clouds, sun and moon discs and stars; HDRP gets it as its sky for reflections and ambient light. Independent of the ray tracing switches.""},""Sky & fog / Clouds and stars"":{""name"":""Sky & fog / Clouds and stars"",""help"":""Volumetric clouds of the weather's cloud types, drifting with its wind, and their shadows on the ground. A map can put a cloud sea into its valleys ([clouds] sea = <height>).""},""Sky & fog / Fog"":{""name"":""Sky & fog / Fog"",""help"":""Fog and haze in 3D from the own engine, lit by the traced sun or moon, the sky and the lamps and headlights; the map's local fog and the tyre smoke are part of it.""},""Sky & fog / HDRP's fog"":{""name"":""Sky & fog / HDRP's fog"",""help"":""Only with Native fog off (HDRP's volumetric fog in its place).""},""Lighting & shadows / Native lighting"":{""name"":""Lighting & shadows / Native lighting"",""help"":""All of the opaque lighting from the own engine: traced sun and moon shadows, lamp and headlight shadows, the sky light and GI, reflections, whatever the ray tracing switches say. Their quality is set below and in Ambient light & GI and Reflections & glass.""},""Lighting & shadows / The game's particles"":{""name"":""Lighting & shadows / The game's particles"",""help"":""The game's and the track's own alpha blended particles (dust, spray, smoke) drawn with NatureFX's particle shader, lit by the own engine's sun or moon, sky and lamps and inside its 3D fog. Fire, sparks and glows keep their own.""},""Lighting & shadows / HDRP's sun shadows"":{""name"":""Lighting & shadows / HDRP's sun shadows"",""help"":""Only with Native lighting off (HDRP's shadow maps in place of the traced shadows).""},""Sun & time / Time of day"":{""name"":""Sun & time / Time of day"",""help"":""""},""Nature / Wind"":{""name"":""Nature / Wind"",""help"":""""},""Weather / Weather"":{""name"":""Weather / Weather"",""help"":""""},""Weather / Season"":{""name"":""Weather / Season"",""help"":""Colours of the trees and grass that the map's profile describes, and the floating particles. Auto: the Autumn and Snow weather, else the map's own season.""},""Weather / Rain and snow"":{""name"":""Weather / Rain and snow"",""help"":""Falling rain and snow around the camera, with the weather: rain streaks that splash where they land and show in headlights and under street lights, drifting snowflakes. 0 turns them off.""},""Road / Road surface"":{""name"":""Road / Road surface"",""help"":""Marks are kept around the camera and cleared when you drive far away.""},""Cars / Headlights"":{""name"":""Cars / Headlights"",""help"":""A real low beam in place of the game's round spot: the lamp's colour and strength, and the beam's sharp cut-off just below the horizon (rising on the kerb side, left: driving on the left), so the road is lit and the eyes above it are not.""},""Cars / Car finish"":{""name"":""Cars / Car finish"",""help"":""Paint reflects like real car paint: a clear varnish mirror over the coloured base. DX12 ray tracing.""},""Cars / Cars in the rain"":{""name"":""Cars / Cars in the rain"",""help"":""Beading drops, water running off and an oily sheen, drawn over the car paint.""},""Cars / Smoke, glow and dirt"":{""name"":""Cars / Smoke, glow and dirt"",""help"":""Volumetric tyre smoke and spray lit by the sun, lamps and headlights (needs Tyre marks on: it starts where the tyres slide). Brake discs that glow after hard braking, afterfire.""},""Reflections & glass / Ray traced reflections"":{""name"":""Reflections & glass / Ray traced reflections"",""help"":""Wet roads, puddles and car paint reflect the whole scene, including what is off screen. DX12 only.""},""Reflections & glass / Glass"":{""name"":""Reflections & glass / Glass"",""help"":""The own engine draws the glass whole: what it lets through (tinted by its colour as far as it is opaque), what it mirrors (traced), the sun's glint and the bend of solid glass. HDRP's glass is hidden meanwhile. Needs Glass reflections.""},""Exposure & tone / Own post-processing"":{""name"":""Exposure & tone / Own post-processing"",""help"":""NatureFX's own exposure (metering and eye adaptation), bloom, tone curve and colour, in place of HDRP's. HDRP's own post-processing, TAA and colour grading are off meanwhile (anti-aliasing: DLSS, else the own TAA).""},""Exposure & tone / Exposure"":{""name"":""Exposure & tone / Exposure"",""help"":""Fixed: one exposure for every scene, like a camera set by hand; eye adaptation brightens shade and tunnels and settles back in sunlight.""},""Exposure & tone / Tone"":{""name"":""Exposure & tone / Tone"",""help"":""""},""DLSS / NVIDIA DLSS"":{""name"":""DLSS / NVIDIA DLSS"",""help"":""Anti-aliasing and upscaling by NatureFX's own engine in place of HDRP's TAA (RTX GPUs; others get the own TAA). Needs Own post-processing (Exposure & tone).""},""Lens & eye / Eye and lens"":{""name"":""Lens & eye / Eye and lens"",""help"":""Night vision: in the dark colours fade towards blue-green and dim parts get grainy, as the eye sees. Lens flare: ghosts and streaks from bright lights. Depth of field: focus on the car, for replays and photos.""},""Ambient light & GI / Ray traced ambient light"":{""name"":""Ambient light & GI / Ray traced ambient light"",""help"":""Light that does not come straight from the sun: darkened where the surroundings block the sky (under cars, roofs and trees, in corners and gaps) and tinted by what it bounces off. The sun light is left to the shadows. DX12 only.""},""Shader rebuild / Shader rebuild"":{""name"":""Shader rebuild / Shader rebuild"",""help"":""NatureFX's own shaders in place of the game's. Replaced materials also enter the ray tracing with their real colour and smoothness.""},""Ray tracing / Ray tracing engine"":{""name"":""Ray tracing / Ray tracing engine"",""help"":""How NatureFX's own engine (NFXNative.dll) traces every ray traced effect (surfaces, shadows, ambient light, lamps, light shafts, reflections). DX12 only.""},""Settings / Interface"":{""name"":""Settings / Interface"",""help"":""""},""Developer / Debug page"":{""name"":""Developer / Debug page"",""help"":""Everything for development is on the debug page now: video memory, GPU and CPU load, the scene and the log, and the developer's switches and tools (ray tracing views, NRD parts, DLSS tests, shader reload, texture budget, shader dumps). Served on this PC only (127.0.0.1): open the address below in a browser (a second screen).""},""Map / Map profile"":{""name"":""Map / Map profile"",""help"":""Per-map settings from the map's nfx_profile object, or kino/config/NatureFX/maps/<scene>.nfx (that file wins). docs/map-authoring.md""},""Map / Lights and reflections"":{""name"":""Map / Lights and reflections"",""help"":""Light markers switch on at dusk or night (Sun > time of day to check).""},""Map / Grass and forest"":{""name"":""Map / Grass and forest"",""help"":""3D grass needs Replace shaders on (Shader rebuild).""},""Map / Ground detail"":{""name"":""Map / Ground detail"",""help"":""Objects take the ground's colour where they stand in it, the profile's painted dirt ([paint]) and debris along the road's edges. Needs the own engine.""},""Map / Effects"":{""name"":""Map / Effects"",""help"":""Decals, puddles and water, local fog and floating particles. Each shows what it is doing or what it waits for.""}}},""ja"":{""settings"":{},""groups"":{},""ui"":{}}}";
	}
}
